{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/834946-modified-detachments","id":834946,"title":"Modified detachments","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-22T04:48:41-08:00","id":834946,"title":"Modified detachments","content":"Inspired by <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/705199-banes-for-breaking-points\">this</a> thread, I made small adjustments to the way humanity and detachments work, in order to make &quot;stabilizing&quot; a bit more likely, and make banes more worthwhile.<br /> <br /> It is available <a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ocfyvptuqlw86ru/Humanity.pdf?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> on my dropbox, since it is too large for the forum's attachment limit. <br /> <br /> All criticism welcome, etc. What I really want to know is if you think the small bit of extra work required to figure out the detachment dice pool is worth using this instead of the breaking point &gt; dice pool list?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T05:30:47-08:00","id":834962,"title":"","content":"All these changes seem fine on their face. However, in my opinion, the added complexity is simply not worth it, in terms of play. Low humanity kindred can stabilize by simply avoiding a couple of breaking points... And higher amount of tables just make the whole thing take more time to resolve.<br /> <br /> Of course, this might be a totally worthwhile exchange on other tables <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T04:05:35-08:00","id":836330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Griautis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/834946-modified-detachments?p=834962#post834962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, this might be a totally worthwhile exchange on other tables <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Naturally, it all comes to the table at hand... I think tables that make a lot of detachment rolls would benefit from this, because those players might adapt to the calculation quickly, and the added &quot;resolution&quot; would increase the depth of many characters. <br /> This is the simplest calculation that came to mind that includes both the breaking point rank and the character's humanity level into account, and I feel it is crucial that any humanity shift includes both. Don't know if I can make it easier with that in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T05:30:14-08:00","id":836363,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure the added complexity to the detachment roll here matters. It would just as easy to give out modifiers than trying to calculate a new formula each time. &quot;Characters who suffer detachment more than 2 difference from their current Humanity take a -1 penalty to the roll. A 5 difference has a -2.&quot; Something like that. Much simpler. <br /> <br /> As for the modifying options? I'm actually not a fan. Customization is done by creating custom triggers and breaking points. Your suggestions imply that just shifting around points is fine. And I'm really really not a fan of ignoring an entire group. That's completely ignoring the point of Humanity by striking out entire things that make you more of a monster and hand waving them away. I find it really a big disconnect that the you can ignore an entire category called Inhumanity on a scale that measures your inhumanity. Ignoring blood bonds is likewise something I'm firmly opposed to. That's a HUGE part of how the vinculum works now, and casually granting immunity to half of it? That's a major change to the game. Ignoring the detachment for learning Cruac is likewise unthematic. <br /> <br /> Why is betraying a cotorie or covenant a detachment? Or attaining Status 5? Ruining someone's life? None of these are inhuman acts. Perhaps vicious and mean, but still very human. It feels very random to have them in the first place. I get the impression its more to fill out the list than anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T05:38:26-08:00","id":836371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/834946-modified-detachments?p=836363#post836363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is betraying a cotorie or covenant a detachment? Or attaining Status 5? Ruining someone's life? None of these are inhuman acts. Perhaps vicious and mean, but still very human. It feels very random to have them in the first place. I get the impression its more to fill out the list than anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gaining Status 5 in a covenant can be under the same justification of gaining Status 1 in a covenant. <br /> <br /> Agree with the rest of your points, tho.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-24T09:19:14-08:00","id":836465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/834946-modified-detachments?p=836363#post836363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'm really really not a fan of ignoring an entire group. That's completely ignoring the point of Humanity by striking out entire things that make you more of a monster and hand waving them away. I find it really a big disconnect that the you can ignore an entire category called Inhumanity on a scale that measures your inhumanity. Ignoring blood bonds is likewise something I'm firmly opposed to. That's a HUGE part of how the vinculum works now, and casually granting immunity to half of it? That's a major change to the game. Ignoring the detachment for learning Cruac is likewise unthematic.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can already take a bane to 'ignore' Vinculum-based breaking points. You can already take a bane to 'ignore' learning Cruac Breaking Points - unless you're seeing a clause somewhere in 2nd Edition that specifically grants exceptions for that rule on those points. The argument about thematics more seems like personal taste and not anything in RAW. I'd say, rather, exploring what it means to be a Kindred in tune with learning Cruac (bane) vs. not has plenty of thematic potential. <br /> <br /> Also, I'd quibble with the idea that taking a permanent bane plus a penalty to all further breaking points of any kind is a handwave. It's a serious negative mechanic to a character, and I'd bet there are a ton of breaking points you would never have a character take a bane to 'ignore.' Without broader categories, you have a rules situation that will never apply to 80% of the listed breaking points. Banes will continue to mostly be taken for violence / murder because they have the most bang for the price.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Boz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/834946-modified-detachments#post834946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All criticism welcome, etc. What I really want to know is if you think the small bit of extra work required to figure out the detachment dice pool is worth using this instead of the breaking point &gt; dice pool list?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would personally stick with the base rules for the detachment pool, but I'm curious on how your formula tussles out in live play. I like a lot of the categories you settled on (especially the headings). Think I'll still split off Violence from Murder, though. <br /> <br /> Exposure feels a little problematic, but this might more be personal as I dislike the concept of deliberate humanity hits between characters (I hate the Nos Merit that allows this) over the idea itself. I tend to force breaking points for others' actions only when the character can but doesn't do something to interfere. If they stand by complicit, I force a check with a +1 or +2 bonus depending on the circumstances. <br /> <br /> I don't think I'd put Frenzy in the lists by themselves, simply because there are a lot of other consequences to frenzy that will likely come through the narrative anyway. Plus they still have to check for any sins committed during the frenzy.<br /> <br /> Other criticisms would simply be quibbles about specific levels here and there.<br /> <br /> Oh, I really love your expanded condition lists for the breaking point process, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T04:38:01-08:00","id":836966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/834946-modified-detachments?p=836465#post836465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can already take a bane to 'ignore' Vinculum-based breaking points. You can already take a bane to 'ignore' learning Cruac Breaking Points - unless you're seeing a clause somewhere in 2nd Edition that specifically grants exceptions for that rule on those points.</div> </div> </div> </div> The section on Banes refers to the breaking points from the Humanity section. The vinculum and Cruac breaking points are outside that scope, as are breaking points from other sources that are just as magically inflicted - someone using Unsettling Gaze on you, for example. The game isn't designed with Banes to shrug off the dangers of other magical forces inflicted on you. I don't see anything that allows it.<br /> <br /> That said, you really seem to be taking criticism of someone else's work here personally, Holy, if you're attacking someone else's reasons for disliking it. I put forwards reasons on why I don't like it, and its somehow wrong and must be shouted down?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 02-25-2016, 07:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T10:10:47-08:00","id":837068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/834946-modified-detachments?p=836966#post836966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The section on Banes refers to the breaking points from the Humanity section. The vinculum and Cruac breaking points are outside that scope, as are breaking points from other sources that are just as magically inflicted - someone using Unsettling Gaze on you, for example. The game isn't designed with Banes to shrug off the dangers of other magical forces inflicted on you. I don't see anything that allows it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a decent point, and nicely sidesteps the issue of taking a bane for Diablerie, which I wouldn't allow. I can see expanding that to the other out-section one-offs (Unsettling Gaze, Embrace, Revenants, etc.) <br /> <br /> Point fails on learning Cruac, however, as its listed as a Humanity 4 sin on the chart directly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/834946-modified-detachments?p=836966#post836966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That said, you really seem to be taking criticism of someone else's work here personally, Holy, if you're attacking someone else's reasons for disliking it. I put forwards reasons on why I don't like it, and its somehow wrong and must be shouted down?</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't attacking you, I wasn't shouting, and pretty sure there's no 'being wrong' on whether or not you like a house rule. I apologize for anything I wrote contrary to that intent. This is a design thread, makes sense to me to talk about multiple viewpoints. Griautis agreed with your points except one and commented. I disagreed with more than that and commented. As for why I felt compelled to say anything, the inspiration thread linked was started by me, so this is a system that I support as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4047-holy","name":"Holy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"274"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}